# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mikołaj Jan Gawkowski et al. (2026). Dyna-Mat: End-to-end benchmarking of foundation machine learning interatomic potentials in finite-temperature ensembles.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2607.03433  arXiv:2607.03433v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2607.03433v1 (sha256 26604caa07fd48ed...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 388 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/gawkowski2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the Dyna-Mat-v1.0 data set (17 NVT first-principles
# MD trajectories at 293-1500 K over metals, TMDs, alloys, perovskites,
# interfaces and molecular crystals; VASP PBE, FHI-aims PBE+D3 for the
# molecular crystals) and the 15 foundation MLIPs evaluated on it as
# distributed, in four tiers of training data. Per-model energy and force
# RMSEs, RDF, pressure and VDOS errors are shown only in figures; the text
# gives only tier medians, which are aggregates over models and are not
# encoded.

