###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Per-model mean energy and force RMSEs over the 17 systems (Fig. 2), per-class errors (Figs. S1-S2) and RDF, pressure and VDOS errors are figure-only. The text states only tier medians (energy 0.236, 0.180, 0.164, 0.116 eV/atom; force 0.166, 0.106, 0.063, 0.054 eV/A for Tiers 1-4), which aggregate several models and have no single model to attach to.
# - MatterSim-v1.0.0-5M is linked to the registry model MatterSim-v1. The MACE-MP-0 release and the EquiformerV2 checkpoint are not named precisely, so they are paper-local runs. The molecular-crystal trajectories use the FHI-aims reference, which the data set node does not separate.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/gawkowski2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
